From: Isaiah <isaiahdw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun8i: do not fail probe on the MAC reset

No PHY is attached at probe time, so a PHY that only outputs its
RGMII clock after driver initialization (Maxio MAE0621A) cannot
satisfy the reset yet. The DMA reset at first open repeats it once
the PHY driver has run.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c	2026-08-09 15:36:15
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c	2026-08-09 15:36:15
@@ -1226,9 +1226,17 @@
 			goto dwmac_mux;
 		}
 	} else {
+		/* With a PHY whose RGMII clock output only starts once its
+		 * driver has initialized it (Maxio MAE0621A), this reset
+		 * cannot succeed yet: no PHY is attached during probe. The
+		 * MAC is reset again by the DMA reset on first open, after
+		 * the PHY driver has run, so do not fail the probe over it.
+		 */
 		ret = sun8i_dwmac_reset(priv);
-		if (ret)
-			goto dwmac_remove;
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "MAC reset deferred to first open\n");
+			ret = 0;
+		}
 	}
 
 	pm_runtime_put(&pdev->dev);
